{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]When I survey the [G]wondrous [D]cross
On [D]which the Prince of [G]glory [D]died [A]
My [D]richest gain I [G]count but [D]loss
And [D]pour con[A]tempt on [C2]all my [D]pride
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D] [G] [D]
[G] [D]
[G]
[D] [A]
[G] [D]
[G] [D]
[G]
[D] [A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For[D]bid it, Lord, that [G]I should [D]boast
Save [D]in the death of [G]Christ my [D]God [A]
All the [D]vain things that [G]charm me [D]most
I [D]sacri[A]fice them [C]to His [D]blood
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]See, from His head, His [G]hands, His [D]feet
[D]Sorrow and love flow [G]mingled [D]down [A]
Did [D]e'er such love and [G]sorrow [D]meet
Or [D]thorns com[A]pose so [C]rich a [D]crown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Were the [D]whole realm of [G]nature [D]mine
That [D]were an offering [G]far too [D]small [A]
Love so a[D]mazing, [G]so di[D]vine
De[D]mands my [A]soul, my [C]life, my [D]all
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
